  enPath="/en/privacy/"
>
  <section style="padding:64px 0">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h1>Legal notice and privacy policy</h1>
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="small muted">
          This is a courtesy translation. The{' '}
          <a href="/privacidad/">Spanish version</a> is the authoritative one and prevails in case of any discrepancy.
        </p>

        <h2>Legal notice</h2>
        <p>
          In compliance with Spanish Law 34/2002 of 11 July, on information society services and electronic commerce,
          the following details are provided:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Owner:</strong> Facundo Corbalán</li>
          <li><strong>Tax ID (NIF):</strong> Z0319658D</li>
          <li><strong>Address:</strong> Obanos 2, bajo B, 28050 Madrid, Madrid, Spain</li>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:facundo@facundocorbalan.com">facundo@facundocorbalan.com</a></li>
          <li>
            <strong>Activity:</strong> IT consulting services in SAP HCM, Payroll and SuccessFactors Employee Central
            Payroll
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Access to this website is free of charge and does not require registration.</p>
        <p>
          Unless stated otherwise, the contents of this website — including text, images, design and other elements —
          belong to Facundo Corbalán or are used with the appropriate authorisation. Their reproduction, distribution,
          public communication or transformation is not permitted without prior authorisation, except where the law
          allows it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The owner endeavours to keep the published information accurate and up to date, but does not guarantee the
          absence of errors and accepts no liability for decisions taken solely on the basis of its contents. Links to
          third-party sites are provided for reference; the owner neither controls nor is responsible for their
          contents, availability or policies.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy policy</h2>

        <h3>1. Data controller</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Facundo Corbalán</strong>, tax ID <strong>Z0319658D</strong>, address{' '}
          <strong>Obanos 2, bajo B, 28050 Madrid, Madrid, Spain</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contact address for privacy matters and for exercising your rights:
          <a href="mailto:facundo@facundocorbalan.com">facundo@facundocorbalan.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Data processed, purpose and legal basis</h3>
        <p>The data processed depends on how you get in touch:</p>

        <h4>Contact form</h4>
        <p>
          Name, email address, company — where provided —, type of service requested, message content and your
          acceptance of this privacy policy.
        </p>
        <p>
          The purpose is to answer your enquiry, assess a possible engagement and, where appropriate, manage the steps
          leading up to a professional relationship. The legal basis is the consent given by ticking the box on the
          form, under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR and, where the enquiry concerns a possible engagement, the pre-contractual
          measures requested by the data subject under Article 6(1)(b) GDPR.
        </p>
        <p>
          The fields marked as required are necessary in order to reply. If they are not provided, the enquiry cannot be
          submitted or properly handled.
        </p>

        <h4>Email, telephone and WhatsApp</h4>
        <p>
          The identifying, contact, professional and project data you choose to provide.
        </p>
        <p>
          The purpose is to handle the communication and, where applicable, to prepare or manage the professional
          relationship. The legal basis is the pre-contractual measures requested by you under Article 6(1)(b) GDPR, or
          the legitimate interest in responding to professional enquiries under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
        </p>
        <p>
          By using WhatsApp you leave this website and access a third-party service. Any processing WhatsApp carries out
          as controller of its own platform is governed by its own terms and privacy policy.
        </p>

        <h4>Call bookings via Calendly</h4>
        <p>
          When booking a call, the following may be processed: name, email address, date and time of the meeting, time
          zone, answers included in the booking and any other information you choose to provide.
        </p>
        <p>
          The purpose is to manage the appointment and its related communications. The legal basis is the
          pre-contractual measures requested by you under Article 6(1)(b) GDPR. Calendly provides the service as a
          processor on behalf of the controller, without prejudice to its own processing as described in its privacy
          policy.
        </p>

        <h4>Browsing and site security</h4>
        <p>
          The hosting provider may process technical data such as IP address, date and time of access, requested
          resource, browser, operating system and security logs.
        </p>
        <p>
          The purpose is to serve the website, maintain its availability, prevent abuse and diagnose incidents. The
          legal basis is the legitimate interest in operating and protecting the site, under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
        </p>
        <p>
          Data is not used for advertising, unsolicited marketing or profiling. No automated decisions producing legal
          or similarly significant effects are made.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Source of the data</h3>
        <p>
          Data comes directly from the data subject when using the form, writing, calling, contacting via WhatsApp or
          booking an appointment. Technical browsing data is generated automatically on accessing the site.
        </p>

        <h3>4. Retention</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Enquiries that do not lead to a professional relationship are kept for a maximum of{' '}
            <strong>one year from the last contact</strong>, unless earlier erasure is requested or retention is
            necessary to bring, exercise or defend claims.
          </li>
          <li>
            Where an enquiry leads to a professional relationship, data is kept for the duration of that relationship
            and, once ended, for the periods needed to comply with legal obligations and address possible liabilities.
          </li>
          <li>
            Technical logs are kept only for as long as needed to provide and protect the service, resolve incidents and
            comply with applicable legal obligations, according to the hosting provider's configuration and retention
            periods.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Data is blocked or deleted once it is no longer necessary, unless a legal retention obligation applies.
        </p>

        <h3>5. Providers, recipients and international transfers</h3>
        <p>
          The following providers are used to deliver the service and may access personal data as processors:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Netlify, Inc.</strong>, for hosting the site and receiving and managing form submissions.</li>
          <li><strong>Microsoft 365</strong>, for professional email.</li>
          <li><strong>Calendly, LLC</strong>, for call bookings.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Data is neither sold nor disclosed to third parties, except where legally required or where necessary to
          bring, exercise or defend claims.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some providers or their sub-processors may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where applicable,
          transfers to the United States rely on the adequacy decision for the{' '}
          <strong>EU-US Data Privacy Framework</strong> for participating entities and, additionally or alternatively,
          on the European Commission's <strong>standard contractual clauses</strong> or other valid safeguards under the
          GDPR.
        </p>
        <p>
          Further information is available in the privacy and data protection documents of{' '}
          <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Netlify</a>,
          <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/privacy/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Microsoft</a> and{' '}
          <a href="https://calendly.com/legal/privacy-notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Calendly</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>6. Google Fonts</h3>
        <p>
          The site's typefaces are loaded from <strong>Google Fonts</strong>. In doing so, the browser connects to
          Google servers and transmits technical data, including the IP address, in order to download the necessary
          files. The purpose is to present the site with a consistent appearance and the legal basis is the legitimate
          interest in providing adequate rendering, under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google may process data outside the European Economic Area in accordance with the transfer mechanisms
          described in its privacy policy. This connection can be avoided in a future version by self-hosting the
          typefaces.
        </p>

        <h3>7. Cookies and similar technologies</h3>
        <p>This site uses no first-party analytics, tracking or advertising cookies.</p>
        <p>
          Browser local storage is used for a single technical purpose: to remember that you have dismissed the notice
          offering the site in the other language. That value stays in your browser, identifies no one and is not sent
          to any server.
        </p>
        <p>
          Links to Calendly, WhatsApp, LinkedIn, Malt, Credly and other external services lead to third-party sites.
          Those services may use cookies or other technologies under their own policies once you access them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Should analytics, advertising or other non-essential technologies be added in the future, this policy and,
          where necessary, the consent mechanism will be updated before they are activated.
        </p>

        <h3>8. Your rights</h3>
        <p>
          You may exercise your rights of <strong>access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction of processing
          and portability</strong> by writing to{' '}
          <a href="mailto:facundo@facundocorbalan.com">facundo@facundocorbalan.com</a>, stating which right you wish to
          exercise. Additional information may be requested only where necessary to verify your identity.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw it at any time by the same means. Withdrawal does not
          affect the lawfulness of processing carried out beforehand.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may also lodge a complaint with the <strong>Spanish Data Protection Agency</strong> at{' '}
          <a href="https://www.aepd.es/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.aepd.es</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>9. Security</h3>
        <p>
          Reasonable technical and organisational measures are applied to protect data against loss, alteration,
          unauthorised access or disclosure. That said, no system connected to the internet can guarantee absolute
          security.
        </p>

        <h3>10. Changes to this policy</h3>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated to reflect legal or technical changes, or changes in the services used. The version
          in force is always the one published on this page.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 2 September 2026.</p>

        <hr />
        <p class="small muted">
          This policy governs only the processing related to the website and its contact channels. Where Facundo
          Corbalán accesses personal data on behalf of a client while providing professional services, he acts as a
          processor and that relationship must be governed by the corresponding contract under Article 28 GDPR.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
